Traps met:
- Someone was using the machine (Chrome frontmost). The harness's
  activation took the focus from them and their keys landed in Detour: a
  stray "ched" in the page's field, an "s" before a typed URL (which then
  ran a search), the page scrolled to 0. The harness now waits for
  `CGEventSource.secondsSinceLastEventType` (HID input only; posted events
  do not count) to show 12 s of idleness before activating or refocusing,
  and logs any human input while it posts a key. A dark dropdown capture
  taken while the person had brought Chrome forward showed their window
  instead and was deleted; phase 2 was run again.
- The harness held the Quick Detour controllers in `guard let` locals, so
  "released" read false; they are held unowned now. (The unit test's
  async variant had the same trap: async frames keep locals alive.)
- Interleaved `chrome.storage.local` get/set in the worker lost events.

